{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8MqpoQGHMf2rxi6E1C3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't get any of this data, so I have no entity numbers, statuses, dates, formation states or agents to give you.\n\nThe California Secretary of State's business search (bizfileonline.sos.ca.gov) is the only official source for these five records. It blocks automated access:\n- My direct query to its search API returned a bot-protection challenge page (Incapsula) instead of data.\n- A normal page fetch returned HTTP 403.\n\nI stopped there and didn't try to get around the block. I also didn't fill in the fields from memory or from third-party aggregators. You asked for official SOS data only, and those fields change, especially status and agent for service of process. Anything I gave you from memory could be wrong, and you'd be relying on it for a signing decision.\n\n**What you can do to get the data:**\n1. Open https://bizfileonline.sos.ca.gov/search/business in a browser.\n2. Search each name. Use the \"Corporation\" filter, and try a shorter name if the exact one returns nothing.\n3. Open each record. The detail view shows the entity number, status, initial filing date, state of formation and agent for service of process.\n4. Look closely at which entity you find:\n   - **Foreign vs. domestic:** These companies are probably Delaware corporations registered in California as foreign corporations. They would show \"Delaware\" as the state of formation and a registration date in California. Anthropic PBC is also a Delaware public benefit corporation.\n   - **Name variations:** Registered names can differ slightly, for example \"Rippling People Center, Inc.\" or \"Notion Labs, Inc.\" with a comma.\n   - **Status:** \"Active\" is what you want. \"Suspended\" or \"FTB Forfeited\" would be a red flag. Check the Statement of Information date as well.\n5. For a certified record, use the SOS's certificate of status service. Counsel often requests this before signing.\n\nIf you paste the five records or save the pages as files, I can check them and put them into a comparison table. If your company has a corporate-records service (CSC, CT Corporation, Cogency), it can pull all five quickly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":19902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316},"output_tokens":637,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"748e09d4-7656-43b5-b9d3-b86efe908ad3","uuid":"4e238408-04f5-42f8-9096-8ecfbca33d06","timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:27:27.644Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8MqpZm4QNDb8Aan4sBa"}
